      "description": "Career Exploration by Class year | Wellesley Career Education Skip to main content MyWellesley Give Handshake Hive Events ELR Getting Started Employers Faculty Parents About Career Advising Career Exploration Arts, Media, & Technology Business, Consulting, Finance, & Marketing Communication, Education, Government, & International Affairs​ Health Professions Advising Pre-Law Advising Science, Public Health, & Behavioral Health Career Essentials Resources Drop-ins & Peer Career Mentors Graduate School Internships Policies Application Support Short Internship Projects (SHIPs) Wellesley-funded Internships & Grants FAQs Fellowships Fellowships for Undergraduates Fellowships for Graduates Class of 2027 Fellowship Planning Fellowships for International Students Fellowships Browser Civic Engagement Ministrare Peer Leader Office Hours Alumnae BEAM Entrepreneurship Advising Make It Make Cents Wellesley in Business Symposium Career Exploration by Class year Career Advising Career Exploration Arts, Media, & Technology Business, Consulting, Finance, & Marketing Communication, Education, Government, & International Affairs​ Health Professions Advising Pre-Law Advising Science, Public Health, & Behavioral Health Career Essentials Resources Drop-ins & Peer Career Mentors Graduate School Internships Policies Application Support Short Internship Projects (SHIPs) Wellesley-funded Internships & Grants FAQs Fellowships Fellowships for Undergraduates Fellowships for Graduates Class of 2027 Fellowship Planning Fellowships for International Students Fellowships Browser Civic Engagement Ministrare Peer Leader Office Hours Alumnae BEAM Entrepreneurship Advising Make It Make Cents Wellesley in Business Symposium Handshake Hive Events Deadlines Resources Recruit About Home Career Exploration by Class year Exploring careers? Start here! Regardless of what year you are at Wellesley, we are here to help you explore potential career paths. Every student is matched with an Advisor for Career Exploration (ACEs), who is available for conversations about your values, strengths, and interests. Your ACE will provide the mentorship, tools, connections, and space for self-assessment and reflection to identify the paths you want to pursue. Schedule an appointment in Handshake to meet with your ACE as follows: First Years & Juniors: Ariane Baker, ACE for the Classes of 2027 & 2029 Sophomores & Seniors: Hayley Meredith, ACE for the Class of 2028 & 2030 Below, we have broken down some of opportunities to get you started in thinking about your career journey. This is not intended to be a comprehensive checklist; rather, think of this as a collection of some of our most frequently referenced resources. Quick links: First Years • Sophomores • Juniors • Seniors Career Essentials: Resumes, Cover Letters, Interviews, & More! Through the Career Essentials workshop series, you will develop skills and the foundational knowledge necessary to navigate career development. Learn about resumes, cover letters, interviewing, informational interviewing, negotiation, and personal statements. Watch the series & explore resources The Wellesley Hive The Wellesley Hive is a digital platform exclusively for the Wellesley community where you can mentor or find mentorship and learn about possible career paths. The Hive is a platform where alumnae and students can ask questions and seek guidance, coach and inspire, and find paths to professional aspirations during one-time conversations or through more long-term mentorship. Explore the Hive Career Exploration Resources The following resources will can help you along your career exploration journey. These resources will be helpful as you attend career fairs, conduct research, identify members of your personal advisory board, and schedule informational interviews or job shadow opportunities. Making the Most of a Virtual Internship or Project 20+ Questions to Jump-start Your Career Exploration Assess Yourself: What Are You Bringing on Your Career Journey? Job Shadowing How to Conduct Career Research How to Use a Career Fair as an Exploration Opportunity Making the Most of a Virtual Internship or Project 20+ Questions to Jump-start Your Career Exploration Assess Yourself: What Are You Bringing on Your Career Journey? Job Shadowing How to Conduct Career Research How to Use a Career Fair as an Exploration Opportunity Hayley Meredith Susan L. Wagner ’82 Associate Director/Advisor for Career Exploration (Classes of 2028 & 2030) hm100@wellesley.edu Make an Appointment Resources for First Years Welcome to Wellesley! As a first-year student, your priority is to explore and try new things academically, personally, and professionally. This is a great time to learn more about yourself and your interests, discover new and exciting options for your future, and build community with your peers! Check out some of our resources below to get you started. But remember, these are just a handful of the opportunities and resources available to you, so keep exploring! You can schedule an appointment with me in Handshake to talk at any time. Select the “Career Exploration, Reflection, and General Guidance” appointment type. Join us for Embark — a First-Year Career Retreat 20+ Questions to Jump-start Your Career Exploration Assess Yourself: What Are You Bringing on Your Career Journey? Career Essentials Summer Hive Internship Projects Campus Research Science Center Summer Research Program Social Science Summer Research Program Knapp Fellows Program in the Social Sciences Wellesley Centers for Women Summer Research Ariane Baker Susan L. Wagner ’82 Associate Director/Advisor for Career Exploration (Classes of 2027 & 2029) as101@wellesley.edu Make an Appointment Resources for Sophomores Sophomore year is a great time to continue your career exploration by trying an internship, research program, or other experiential learning opportunity! This is also your year for major declaration and study abroad considerations, which we are always happy to discuss with you. Below are some suggested resources to help you explore different opportunities. Remember, these are just a handful of the opportunities and resources available to you, so keep exploring! You can schedule an appointment with me in Handshake to talk at any time. Select the “Career Exploration, Reflection, and General Guidance” appointment type. Learn about Career Essentials Don’t forget to explore our various Industry Advising resources , and to sign up for industry-specific newsletters by editing the “Career Interests” section in Handshake. Career Education Signature Internships Wellesley Grants Program Other College & Employer-Sponsored Internships McNair Scholars Program Mellon Mays Undergraduate Fellowship Program Study Abroad and resources from the Office of International Study Mentorship Affinity Pods (MAP) Program Campus Research Science Center Summer Research Program Sophomore Early Research Program Social Science Summer Research Program Knapp Fellows Program in the Social Sciences Wellesley Centers for Women Summer Research Hayley Meredith Susan L. Wagner ’82 Associate Director/Advisor for Career Exploration (Classes of 2028 & 2030) hm100@wellesley.edu Make an Appointment Resources for Juniors Junior year is an exciting time with lots of opportunities available to you for exploration, internships and research, and further reflection on how you might like your post-Wellesley life to look. I am here to help with it all! Below are some suggested resources to help you start to explore what’s possible in your junior year. Let’s be in touch any time to discuss these opportunities and more! You can schedule an appointment with me in Handshake to talk at any time. Select the “Career Exploration, Reflection, and General Guidance” appointment type. Don’t forget to explore our various Industry Advising resources , and to sign up for industry-specific newsletters by editing the “Career Interests” section in Handshake. Learn the Career Essentials Career Education Signature Internships Wellesley Grants Program Other College & Employer-Sponsored Internships Ready, Set, Senior: Resources and event specifically for juniors (aka soon-to-be seniors) Fellowships & Scholarships : Junior year is an essential time to explore the possibilities! Wellesley in Washington summer internship program The Albright Institute Mentorship Affinity Pods (MAP) Program Campus Research Science Center Summer Research Program Social Science Summer Research Program Knapp Fellows Program in the Social Sciences Wellesley Centers for Women Summer Research ​ Ariane Baker Susan L. Wagner ’82 Associate Director/Advisor for Career Exploration (Classes of 2027 & 2029) as101@wellesley.edu Make an Appointment Resources for Seniors Senior year can be an exciting and hectic time to navigate. From participating in special traditions, to soaking up final classes and rhythms of life at Wellesley, to taking steps toward pursuing whatever might come next, it can be tricky to balance it all. This is a great time to take advantage of the resources available to you through Career Education. Whether you’re hoping to attend graduate or professional school, conduct a job search, or find a gap year(s) opportunity (to name a few possible next steps), your ACE and the Industry Advisors are here to support you along the way. Our team is ready to walk alongside you as you prepare to transition to life after Wellesley, whether you have a clear sense of direction or still feel unsure about what to pursue next. Check out some of the resources below to start exploring what senior year has to offer. You can schedule an appointment with me in Handshake to talk at any time. Select the “Career Exploration, Reflection, and General Guidance” appointment type. Remember: after leaving Wellesley, you will still have access to Career Education advising for life as an alum ! Don’t forget to explore our various Industry Advising resources , and to sign up for industry-specific newsletters by editing the “Career Interests” section in Handshake. Mentorship Affinity Pods (MAP) Program Learn the Career Essentials Graduate school resources Fellowships & Scholarships Sign up for The Wellesley Hive to make connections with alums The Albright Institute Check out our fall event, Launch: A Guide to Life After College , and other resources for your life after Wellesley Let’s Talk Contact T. (781) 283-2352 careereducation@wellesley.edu Modulars 400 ( temporary for 2025-2026) 106 Central Street Wellesley, MA 02481 Career Education is available for virtual and in-person appointments . Employers: please visit our recruiting landing page and email recruiting@wellesley.edu with questions. Handshake Disclaimer & Employer Policies Copyright © Trustees of Wellesley College Terms of Use Privacy Policy Press Donate to the Program Handshake Hive Instagram Facebook Linkedin"
    },
