    "https://www.wellesley.edu/careereducation/alumnae": {
      "title": "Career Advancement",
      "description": "Career Advancement | Wellesley Career Education Skip to main content MyWellesley Give Handshake Hive Events ELR Getting Started Employers Faculty Parents About Career Advising Career Exploration Arts, Media, & Technology Business, Consulting, Finance, & Marketing Communication, Education, Government, & International Affairs​ Health Professions Advising Pre-Law Advising Science, Public Health, & Behavioral Health Career Essentials Resources Drop-ins & Peer Career Mentors Graduate School Internships Policies Application Support Short Internship Projects (SHIPs) Wellesley-funded Internships & Grants FAQs Fellowships Fellowships for Undergraduates Fellowships for Graduates Class of 2027 Fellowship Planning Fellowships for International Students Fellowships Browser Civic Engagement Ministrare Peer Leader Office Hours Alumnae BEAM Entrepreneurship Advising Make It Make Cents Wellesley in Business Symposium Career Advancement Career Advising Career Exploration Arts, Media, & Technology Business, Consulting, Finance, & Marketing Communication, Education, Government, & International Affairs​ Health Professions Advising Pre-Law Advising Science, Public Health, & Behavioral Health Career Essentials Resources Drop-ins & Peer Career Mentors Graduate School Internships Policies Application Support Short Internship Projects (SHIPs) Wellesley-funded Internships & Grants FAQs Fellowships Fellowships for Undergraduates Fellowships for Graduates Class of 2027 Fellowship Planning Fellowships for International Students Fellowships Browser Civic Engagement Ministrare Peer Leader Office Hours Alumnae BEAM Entrepreneurship Advising Make It Make Cents Wellesley in Business Symposium Handshake Hive Events Deadlines Resources Recruit About Home Career Advancement Fireside Chat with Lulu Chow Wang alumnae event, organized by New York Wellesley Club Careers. Photograph by Gabriella Reubins. Lifetime Support for Career Advancement A benefit of being a graduate of Wellesley College is continued access to Career Education resources. Dedicated Alumnae Career Advisors and Industry Advisors are here to help you navigate your career journey, make meaningful connections, overcome obstacles, and celebrate success at every stage. We offer one-on-one advising, resume and cover letter reviews, interview practice, professional development webinars, and advice on new trends that will impact your job search process. Our experienced staff can work with you to address whatever you are facing, including making a career pivot/change, advancing in your current career field, re-entering the workforce, or finding an “encore career” after retirement. Connect using Handshake and The Wellesley Hive Alumnae maintain lifelong access to Career Education technology platforms. Handshake is Wellesley's online platform for finding jobs/internships and making appointments with advisors. The Wellesley Hive is an interactive virtual space for professional networking and mentorship with other Wellesley alums and current students. The Hive also includes a robust job board! Each job post features suggested connections to help you take your search to the next level. Find a good job match? Reach out to an alum associated with the role or company. Alums can also share opportunities directly with other alums by posting positions directly to The Hive. For ease of use and security, your Wellesley username and password are required to log in to both platforms. Reset Your Wellesley Login Opportunities for Alums to Engage with Students via Internships Interested in creating an internship for a Wellesley student, or sharing an existing opportunity with the Wellesley network? This helpful resource outlines how. Learn More Spring 2026 Alumnae Connections Programs ‘Ask a Career Coach’ Series Wednesday, January 14, Noon – 1:00 PM ET Tuesday, 3 February, Noon – 1:00 PM ET Monday, March 9, Noon – 1:00 PM ET Thursday, April 2, Noon – 1:00 PM ET (Topic: Fellowships and planning for future graduate and professional studies) Tuesday, May 5, Noon – 1:00 PM ET Whether you're looking for a new industry or position, contemplating graduate study, navigating a role change or promotion, returning to the workforce, or planning for an engaged retirement, drop in to ask our Alum Career Advisors your questions! No need to register — join us on Zoom! Alum Webinar: Thriving and Growing in your Early Career The transition from college to your first job (and second and third jobs) can be challenging and exciting in many ways. In this January 26, 2026 webinar, alum advisors Becky King and Dana Keep shared ideas and tools to help when you are new to a role, what to do if you don’t like your job, and how to keep growing, learning, and advancing in your early career. Watch the recording Alum Webinar: Careers in Human Resources Panel Tuesday, February 24, 2026, Noon – 1:00 PM EST Are you a people person? Interested in hearing from Wellesley alums about a variety of career paths in Human Resources? Join us for this panel discussion to learn more about roles in human resources, talent development, and change management. Watch the recording Fireside Chat: How to remain hopeful and positive during turbulent times Tuesday, March 24, 2026, Noon – 1:00 PM ET Given today’s ever-shifting economic landscape, career resilience is no longer just a soft skill – it’s a necessity. For dedicated professionals, uncertainty can take many forms, from layoffs and market shifts to the impact of AI. We will come together (virtually) to share ideas and strategies for developing adaptability and a growth mindset to approach current and future challenges. Join Career Education and your Wellesley siblings in a supportive and timely conversation. Register Here ‘Designing Your Work Life’ Cohorts This program is for alums who want to make a professional change, but need inspiration to figure out what that might be. Alumnae Career Advisors Dana Keep and Becky King will facilitate the discussion as a group of Wellesley alums help each other ‘build their way forward’ and design a new direction. Space is limited, and we kindly request that participants commit to all three sessions to ensure cohesiveness and continuity of conversation. Tuesdays, April 7, 14, 21 2026, Noon – 1:30 ET (note earlier start date) Email Dana Keep with interest (dkeep@wellesley.edu) Alum Career Book Club: Transitions by William Bridges Thursday, May 14, 2026 Noon – 1:00 PM ET Celebrating 40 years of the best-selling guide for coping with life's changes, Transitions was named one of the 50 all-time best books in self-help and personal development. Aimed at today's current workers and organizations facing unprecedented change, Transitions takes readers step-by-step through the three perilous stages of any transition, explaining how each stage can be understood and embraced. Register Here Alumnae Career Advancement Team Destiny M. Barletta Director, Alumnae Connections Dana Keep Alumnae Career Advisor Becky King Alumnae Career Advisor Alumnae Career Advisors are here for one-on-one advising about career pivots, re-entry into the workforce, resume and cover letter reviews, interview practice, and more. You can schedule an appointment to meet with an Alumnae Career Advisor through Handshake using your Wellesley credentials. Make an Appointment Industry-Specific Advisors Hebert Labbate Susan L. Wagner ’82 Associate Director/Advisor for Communication, Education, Government, & International Affairs Hilda Lief Susan L. Wagner ’82 Associate Director/Advisor for Business, Consulting, Finance, & Marketing Nicole D. Park Susan L. Wagner ’82 Associate Director/Advisor for Pre-Law Cindy Seltzer, Ed.D., MBA Helen Wallace ’33 Director, Health Professions Advising Alexis Trench Susan L. Wagner ’82 Associate Director/Advisor for Science, Behavioral Health, & Public Health Career Education's Industry-specific Advisors can provide industry expertise for alumnae exploring specific career paths, whether looking to break into a new field or advance in their industries with a competitive edge. Make an appointment on Handshake using your Wellesley credentials. Make an Appointment Resources Our advisors have written a series of resources to jumpstart your research on a variety of career topics. Browse the links below, and schedule an appointment in Handshake to explore further! Alumnae Resume Guidelines Career Assessment and Advancement Introduction to Fellowships for Graduates Job Searching After 50 Rejoining the Workforce Up Skill Resources for Alumnae The Wellesley Hive Mentor Resource: The Fundamentals of Successful Mentoring The Wellesley Hive Mentee Resource: What is Mentorship? Alumnae Resume Guidelines Career Assessment and Advancement Introduction to Fellowships for Graduates Job Searching After 50 Rejoining the Workforce Up Skill Resources for Alumnae The Wellesley Hive Mentor Resource: The Fundamentals of Successful Mentoring The Wellesley Hive Mentee Resource: What is Mentorship? Alumnae Webinars Wellesley Career Education hosts professional development webinars to support alums at every career stage, often in partnership with alumnae who offer expertise on a specific topic. An archive of past webinars is housed below. You can also watch a full playlist of our Alum Webinars on Youtube! Expand Related Resources Navigating Small Business Ownership (Webinar, April 2025) Strengthening Your Communication Skills (Webinar, March 2024) Introduction to Chat GPT with Supriya Bhuwalka ’96 (February 2024) LinkedIn Toolbox Workshop with Susan Wojewoda ’96 (Webinar, October 2023) Navigating Disability in the Workplace with Tere Remos '93 (Feb 2023 Webinar) The Lost Art of Connecting: A Virtual Conversation with Susan McPherson (November 2022 Webinar) Projecting Leadership with Intention from Day One with Maya Dolgin ’10 (Webinar, February 2022) Career Book Club: “Switchers” by Dr. Dawn Graham (Webinar, October 2021) Hiring is a Two Way Street (Webinar, May 2021) Women and Financial Literacy (Webinar, April 2021) Preparing for Corporate Board Service (BLC Webinar, March 2021) Spring Forward with Superpowers, Strengths, and Confidence (Webinar, March 2021) Post-Pandemic Reinvention (Webinar, February 2021) Returning to Work After a Career Break Webinar (Webinar, December 2020) 5 Ways to Tell if Consulting is for You — or if it’s not! (November 2020 Webinar) Dreaming of Writing a Book? A Book Coach Shows You How to Stop Wishing And Start Writing (Webinar, November 2020) Is It Time to Redesign Your Job or Career? (Webinar, June 2020) Projecting Professionalism, Clarity, & Confidence on Virtual Platforms (Webinar, May 2020) Networking Matters: Building Authentic & Effective Professional Relationships (Webinar, December 2019) Journey to the Boardroom (Webinar, March 2019) Vacation Time: how the way you travel can change the way you work (Webinar, March 2019) Maternal Optimism: Navigating Work & Parenthood (Webinar, November 2019) The Power of Nonprofit Board Service (October 2019 Webinar) Advancing Your Career Through Gender Equality with Fairygodboss (Webinar, October 2018) Reimagining Retirement with Connie Baher ’63 (Webinar, October 2018) Panel on Mutual Fund Boards of Directors  (Webinar, January 2018) Writing a Fellowships Proposal Webinar Introduction to Chat GPT with Supriya Bhuwalka ’96 (February 2024) Alumnae Career Conversations Wellesley Career Education regularly hosts career conversations with alums across a range of industries, who have generously offered to share their professional experiences with students and other alums. Recordings of many of these webinars are listed below. Expand Related Resources Alumnae Career Conversation with Daena Title ’79 (Webinar, November 2023) Entrepreneurship & Branding: Alumnae Career Conversation with Dawn Nadeau ’95 (Webinar, October 2023) Insights Into Clinical Psychology: Alumnae Career Conversation with Amy Crowe ’78 (March 2023 Webinar) Expanding the Definition of Women in Technology: Career Chat with Cecilia Harvey ’00, Founder and Chair of Tech Women Today (Webinar, June 2023) Branding and Marketing Insights: Alumnae Career Conversation with Sara Gaviser Leslie ’95 (Webinar, October 2022) Architecture Insights: Alumnae Career Conversation with Ann Beha ’72 and Hannah Ahlblad ’14 (Webinar, November 2021) Creating the Contemporary Art Gallery: Alumnae Career Conversation with Milly Glimcher ’61 and Lisa Fischman, Ruth Gordon Shapiro ’37 Director and Chief Curator, Davis Museum (Webinar, November 2021) Inside the NYC Mayor’s Office: Alumnae Career Conversation with Bess Chiu ’03 (Webinar, April 2021) Alumnae Career Conversation: Anne Dickinson Meltz '16 (Wayfair); Elizabeth Good '09 (Wayfair); Hayden Broberg '14 (Insurify) (Webinar, May 2020) Journeys in Finance: Alumnae Career Conversation (Webinar, May 2020) Paper Saver: Alumnae Career Conversation with Mary French ’09, Book Conservator (Recorded Talk, April 2018) Mentor Students & Connect with the Wellesley network! The Wellesley Hive is a flexible, interactive virtual space for professional networking and mentorship. Through this Wellesley-exclusive platform, you can connect with alums and students as a mentor, mentee, or both. Log in to the Wellesley Hive using your Wellesley credentials, and follow the guided process to customize your involvement and improve your connections. Join the Hive Wellesley Hive Members 5,500 + Alums and students are connected to The Wellesley Hive, Wellesley’s Mentorship Platform Global Mentorship 60 + Countries with members connected to The Wellesley Hive Fellowships for Alumnae Fellowships serve as an investment in individuals, for opportunities like: • studying a language • conducting academic research • completing a service project • pursuing graduate study • designing and executing an independent project As an alumna, you still have access to Wellesley Fellowship Program resources and advice from our team. Let us help you make the most of them! Explore Fellowship Opportunities for Alumnae Deadlines Events Jobs/Internships Resources Stories #accounting/insurance #advancement #amt #architecture #biotech/lifescience #careeredplacements #coverletter #exploring #faculty/staff #fellowshipstoolkit #highereducation #law #medschool #selfreflection #students #arts/design #bcfm #business/operations #careerpivot #datascience #employers #explore/try #government #gradschool #internshipgrants #interview #preparing #socialsciences #undergraduatefellowship #applying #cegia #consulting #encorecareer #engineering #entertainment #fundedinternship #gettingstarted #internationalaffairs #lawschool #linkedin #postgraduatefellowship #wellesleyopportunity #civicengagement #entrepreneurship #fundraising #industryexpertise #internationalstudent #k12education #law #negotiation #physicalscience #researchingoptions #distinctpopulations #finance #freelance #mentorship #networking #othereducation #publichealth #research/gradschool #sbp #understandingmyself #behavioralhealth #careerexploration #healthprofessions #management/hr #politics/advocacy #rejoiningtheworkforce #research #resume #servicefellowship #fellowships #marketing #media/pr #publishing #studyabroad #sustainability #travelfellowship #nonprofit #reflection #thinktank #professionalism #technology #writing/editing #recruit #socialmedia #careeressentials #socialscience #arts/humanities #science #careeradvancement #Resource Tags – Internships & Grants #Resource Tags - Faculty & Staff #Resource Tags - Recruiting #Other Tags - for grouping purposes only #Resource Tags - Pre-Law #Resource Tags - Communications, Education, Government, International Affairs #Resource Tags - Alumnae #Resource Tags - Science, Behavioral Health, Public Health #Resource Tags - Career Essentials & Exploration #Resource Tags - Health Professions #Resource Tags - Business, Consulting, Finance, Marketing #Resource Tags - Arts, Media, Technology #Resource Tags - Industry Advising #Resource Tags - Career Exploration #Resource Tags - Grad School #Resource Tags - Fellowships & Scholarships Popular Tags #advancement #industryexpertise #rejoiningtheworkforce #encorecareer #mentorship #postgraduatefellowship Rejoining the Workforce Destiny M. Barletta Many women find it challenging to prepare a resume after being home for several years. Do not discount the value of work that you have been doing, even if it has not been a formal or paid job. This resource will provide an overview for women returning to the workforce and working parents. Read More Journey to the Boardroom (Webinar, March 2019) More Job Searching After 50 Destiny M. Barletta This resource outlines considerations for job searching over 50, including tailored advice for your writing your resume, networking, and interviewing. Read More Advancing Your Career Through Gender Equality with Fairygodboss (Webinar, October 2018) More Introduction to Fellowships for Graduates Kate Dailinger Fellowships and scholarships can fund graduate or professional study, purposeful travel, professional placements, self-designed projects, and so much more. They can help you build your experience and qualifications, help you explore a passion, and clarify a path forward. What would you do with a fellowship? Read More Career Assessment and Advancement Destiny M. Barletta Career Advancement can mean different things to different people. For some, advancement means reaching a leadership position within a company or a field. For others, advancement means performing at a high level in a given role. Sometimes, advancement means switching careers entirely to learn a whole new domain, or focusing on giving back to a field or a community. Read More Load more Let’s Talk Contact T. (781) 283-2352 careereducation@wellesley.edu Modulars 400 ( temporary for 2025-2026) 106 Central Street Wellesley, MA 02481 Career Education is available for virtual and in-person appointments . Employers: please visit our recruiting landing page and email recruiting@wellesley.edu with questions. Handshake Disclaimer & Employer Policies Copyright © Trustees of Wellesley College Terms of Use Privacy Policy Press Donate to the Program Handshake Hive Instagram Facebook Linkedin"
