    "https://www.wellesley.edu/careereducation/gradschool": {
      "title": "Exploring Graduate School",
      "description": "Exploring Graduate School | Wellesley Career Education Skip to main content MyWellesley Give Handshake Hive Events ELR Getting Started Employers Faculty Parents About Career Advising Career Exploration Arts, Media, & Technology Business, Consulting, Finance, & Marketing Communication, Education, Government, & International Affairs​ Health Professions Advising Pre-Law Advising Science, Public Health, & Behavioral Health Career Essentials Resources Drop-ins & Peer Career Mentors Graduate School Internships Policies Application Support Short Internship Projects (SHIPs) Wellesley-funded Internships & Grants FAQs Fellowships Fellowships for Undergraduates Fellowships for Graduates Class of 2027 Fellowship Planning Fellowships for International Students Fellowships Browser Civic Engagement Ministrare Peer Leader Office Hours Alumnae BEAM Entrepreneurship Advising Make It Make Cents Wellesley in Business Symposium Exploring Graduate School Career Advising Career Exploration Arts, Media, & Technology Business, Consulting, Finance, & Marketing Communication, Education, Government, & International Affairs​ Health Professions Advising Pre-Law Advising Science, Public Health, & Behavioral Health Career Essentials Resources Drop-ins & Peer Career Mentors Graduate School Internships Policies Application Support Short Internship Projects (SHIPs) Wellesley-funded Internships & Grants FAQs Fellowships Fellowships for Undergraduates Fellowships for Graduates Class of 2027 Fellowship Planning Fellowships for International Students Fellowships Browser Civic Engagement Ministrare Peer Leader Office Hours Alumnae BEAM Entrepreneurship Advising Make It Make Cents Wellesley in Business Symposium Handshake Hive Events Deadlines Resources Recruit About Home Exploring Graduate School Considering Graduate School? Begin here! Graduate school is an opportunity to examine a field of your choice with more specificity and direction, and it can provide you with the tools you need to succeed in the industry of your choice. Preparation for grad school can begin as early as your first year of college as you begin conversations with your Advisor for Career Exploration about how your values, interests, and strengths align with potential fields of study. Review the resource linked below to develop a concrete understanding of the graduate programs you are interested in. From there, we welcome you to make an appointment in Handshake with the relevant industry-specific Advisor who will support you in the application process. We look forward to talking with you! Graduate School: From Considering to Applying Our Graduate School resource will help you to learn about what graduate school is, how to determine if and when you pursue a graduate degree, how to plan for it, and how to apply! Read More Test Preparation Book Loan Program Wellesley Career Education has LSAT, GRE, MCAT and DAT test prep books to lend to current students planning to take one of these exams in the near term. These materials are intended for current students actively preparing for an LSAT, GRE, MCAT or DAT exam on a set date. Learn more through the link below! Learn More Princeton Review: Discounted Test Preparation We are pleased to have a partnership with Princeton Review that enables Wellesley students and alumnae to purchase test review products at a discount! There are discounted options to help you prepare for the DAT, GMAT, GRE, MCAT, and LSAT. This discount is only available on orders placed through Career Education — learn more through the link below! Learn More Law School Is law school right for you? This resource will help you to consider if, and when, you might go to law school, and the careers that law school can prepare you for. Additionally, you'll learn more about academic & experiential preparation in advance of applying, and the application components.​ In addition to reviewing this resource, you may find it useful to meet with Nicole Park, Career Education's Pre Law Advisor. Students and alumnae can book an appointment with Nicole in Handshake . Learn More Medical School & Health Professions Advising Career Education's Health Professions Advising team is available to support you as you explore clinical care across a variety of patient-facing roles, including: nursing, dentistry, veterinary medicine, medicine, physical therapy, speech language pathology, physician assistant, podiatry, pharmacy, and more. We encourage you to review our resources first to learn more, whether you are exploring, preparing, or applying within the health professions. Learn More Let’s Talk Contact T. (781) 283-2352 careereducation@wellesley.edu Modulars 400 ( temporary for 2025-2026) 106 Central Street Wellesley, MA 02481 Career Education is available for virtual and in-person appointments . Employers: please visit our recruiting landing page and email recruiting@wellesley.edu with questions. Handshake Disclaimer & Employer Policies Copyright © Trustees of Wellesley College Terms of Use Privacy Policy Press Donate to the Program Handshake Hive Instagram Facebook Linkedin"
    },
    "https://www.wellesley.edu/careereducation/fellowships-and-scholarships": {
      "title": "Fellowships & Scholarships",
      "description": "Fellowships & Scholarships | Wellesley Career Education Skip to main content MyWellesley Give Handshake Hive Events ELR Getting Started Employers Faculty Parents About Career Advising Career Exploration Arts, Media, & Technology Business, Consulting, Finance, & Marketing Communication, Education, Government, & International Affairs​ Health Professions Advising Pre-Law Advising Science, Public Health, & Behavioral Health Career Essentials Resources Drop-ins & Peer Career Mentors Graduate School Internships Policies Application Support Short Internship Projects (SHIPs) Wellesley-funded Internships & Grants FAQs Fellowships Fellowships for Undergraduates Fellowships for Graduates Class of 2027 Fellowship Planning Fellowships for International Students Fellowships Browser Civic Engagement Ministrare Peer Leader Office Hours Alumnae BEAM Entrepreneurship Advising Make It Make Cents Wellesley in Business Symposium Fellowships & Scholarships Career Advising Career Exploration Arts, Media, & Technology Business, Consulting, Finance, & Marketing Communication, Education, Government, & International Affairs​ Health Professions Advising Pre-Law Advising Science, Public Health, & Behavioral Health Career Essentials Resources Drop-ins & Peer Career Mentors Graduate School Internships Policies Application Support Short Internship Projects (SHIPs) Wellesley-funded Internships & Grants FAQs Fellowships Fellowships for Undergraduates Fellowships for Graduates Class of 2027 Fellowship Planning Fellowships for International Students Fellowships Browser Civic Engagement Ministrare Peer Leader Office Hours Alumnae BEAM Entrepreneurship Advising Make It Make Cents Wellesley in Business Symposium Handshake Hive Events Deadlines Resources Recruit About Home Fellowships & Scholarships Anne Shen '17, 2016 Barry Goldwater Scholarship and Fulbright recipient. Fellowships & Scholarships Fellowships, broadly defined, fund purposeful activity. To be more specific, fellowships can fund (among other things) language study abroad, undergraduate and postgraduate research, service opportunities, graduate and professional study, independent projects, teaching (both in the U.S. and abroad)... the possibilities are endless, which can be both inspiring and intimidating! Career Education and the Fellowships team are here to help you navigate, no matter where you’re starting or where you hope to go. So how can we help? Smart and capable as you are, you don't have to go it alone! The Fellowships team is here all year 'round, including over the summer, and happy to help you explore fellowships, brainstorm ideas, review drafts , choose recommenders, prep for interviews, and much more. Book a fellowships appointment now-- we can't wait to talk with you! But wait, there's more: Fellowships virtual drop-ins, workshops, and panels happen throughout the calendar year : check out our events listings ! ... Planning to apply for a postgaduate fellowship this fall? Opt-in by May 21 for special access to even more appointments over the summer with our Postgrad Fellowships Summer Prep!  Simply submit this worksheet to this google form by noon (12:00 pm EST) on May 21. We look forward to working with you! … Not sure where to start thinking about postgrad plans?  Try this Visions & Values exercise , and use this fillable Timeline and Materials template to begin to organize your plans! ... Help us celebrate Wellesley nominees, finalists, alternates, honorable mentions, and awardees of fellowships! Will your name be next on our list? ... You Are Here | Common Starting Places | Toolkit You Are Here (And we’re here to help!) There’s no wrong place to start a fellowships search. You may have an idea of what you might like to do; you may wonder what fellowships are available to you; or you might have no idea even what questions to ask! We have resources for no matter where you are in the fellowships process. First things first... I am a... • Undergraduate • Graduate • International student I am looking for a fellowship to support… Browse fellowships by topic, including: ​• Undergraduate research • Graduate or professional degrees/ research study ​• Travel ​• Service ​• Teaching ​• Language study/study abroad Common Starting Places Kate Dailinger Director, Fellowships Caitlin Roberts-Donovan Senior Assistant Director, Fellowships I don’t know where to begin. This is a great place to start. (After all, no one spontaneously becomes a fellowships expert!) Suggestions for where to start exploring and learning more Explore possibilities by major or interest. Peruse the fellowships browser. Make an appointment via Handshake: we would love to meet you, learn more about your interests, and start a conversation about which fellowships might be a good fit (you can also drop by our Virtual Pop-up advising—listings in Handshake ). I don’t know what I want to do after graduation. We completely understand (believe us: from personal experience, we understand) that often it can feel like everyone but you has a plan for after graduation. The truth, though, is the quiet majority aren’t certain about what comes next. Fellowships can provide amazing opportunities postgrad! Fellowships for graduates Check out our resource for graduates . Look through our fellowships browser . ​ ​ You can filter by \"seniors\" to see a variety of options for after graduation, including grad/professional school scholarships, travel fellowships, service fellowships, teaching fellowships, and more. Make an appointment via Handshake: we would love to meet you, learn more about your interests, and start a conversation about which fellowships might be a good fit for what you might like to do next (you can also drop by our Virtual Pop-up advising—listings in Handshake ). You can also book a general career advising appointment with other members of the Career Education team. I could never get a fellowship– why even bother looking into them? Here’s the truth: there is no platonic ideal of a fellowships candidate, and no one could be an equally strong (or equally weak!) candidate for every fellowship. Fellowships are all about fit and feasibility : are you a good fit for what a program is looking for, is it a good fit for you, and is what you’re proposing to do feasible? We’re here to help you navigate those questions. Some things to keep in mind The only way to 100% guarantee that you won’t get a fellowship is if you don’t apply . Our promise to you is that we’ll be honest: if something you’re looking at isn’t a very good fit, we’ll be happy to talk it through with you. Many people are worried about GPA—but many fellowships do not have a minimum GPA requirement . Even when grades do factor into an application, they are just one of many things considered: essays, resumes and experience, and letters of recommendation make up a much more complete picture of a candidate. Exploring fellowships doesn’t lock you in to anything, and you don’t have to have the next ten years of your life planned out in order to apply. I’ve already graduated (perhaps a while ago). Is it too late for me to apply for a fellowship? It is never too late to apply for a fellowship. While it is true that some fellowships are only available to graduating seniors, many more are evergreen opportunities—whether you graduated months, years, or decades ago! If you’re not sure where to get started, here are some helpful tips: Postgraduate Fellowship Exploration Check out our resource for graduates. Look through our fellowships browser ​ You can filter by \"alums\" under \"class year\" to see a variety of options, including grad/professional school scholarships, travel fellowships, service fellowships, teaching fellowships, and more. Make an appointment via Handshake: we would love to meet you, learn more about your interests, and start a conversation about which fellowships might be a good fit for what you might like to do next (you can also drop by our Virtual Pop-up advising—listings in Handshake ) You can also book a general career advising appointment with other members of the Career Education team, like an Alumnae Advisor. I know what I want to do, but I’m not sure how I can get there. The good news is that there are potentially a lot of different ways for fellowships to support what you’d like to do, and we’re here to help you figure out your options! Begin with your interests Explore possibilities by major, activity, or international student status. Make an appointment via Handshake: we would love to meet you, learn more about your interests, and strategize about which fellowships might help you reach your goals (you can also drop by our Virtual Pop-up advising—listings in Handshake ). You can also make an appointment to talk with your Advisor for Career Exploration (ACE) or Alumnae Advisors to see what other paths there might be towards your goals. I’ve heard of [insert name of fellowship!] and think it sounds interesting, but I’m not sure where to start. Excellent! This is a great chance not just to look at the fellowship you’re interested in, but also potentially others. One of the best things about fellowships is that the work you put in to one application is a huge help for other potential applications in the future: Let's dig deeper Many fellowships have resources on the Fellowships & Scholarships page, where you can learn more about requirements, timelines, application materials, and other details. Did you know? There are many more fellowships out there that do not have resources on our website, because you apply for them directly (that is, not through Wellesley). The fellowships team is always happy to help with any fellowship application, whether it’s a Wellesley opportunity or not! Look through the fellowships browser and explore by opportunity type (i.e. travel, service, etc.). Are any of them similar to what you’re looking at, sparking similar interest…? Make an appointment via Handshake: we’d love to meet you and talk about the fellowships process, what might be a good fit, and what your next steps might be. I want to apply for [insert name of fellowship or fellowships] ​Great! Let's get going Many fellowships have resources on the Fellowships & Scholarships page, where you can learn more about requirements, timelines, application materials, and other details. Did you know? There are many more fellowships out there that do not have resources on our website, because you apply for them directly (that is, not through Wellesley). The fellowships team is always happy to help with any fellowship application, whether it’s a Wellesley opportunity or not! Check out our toolkit and sample timelines to get a sense of how the application process might shape up. Make an appointment via Handshake: Did you know that the Fellowships team doesn’t just advise? We can do draft review, help you build timelines, and strategize about your applications as well. Toolkit Deadlines Looking thruogh our fellowships browser listings is a great way to explore possibilities and stay on top of timelines. Filter by opportunity type, citizenship, class year, and more! Browse fellowships Personal Statements A personal statement is a narrative essay that connects your background, experiences, and goals to the mission, requirements, and desired outcomes of the specific opportunity you are seeking. Learn more about this key component to many fellowship applications by watching our webinar or through the written resource below. Learn More Requesting References We recommend that you allow at least eight weeks for a recommender to prepare a letter of reference, and we offer tips to help. Learn More Writing your Resume or CV Resumes and CVs ( curriculum vitaes ) are documents that clearly presents your current and past experiences and accomplishments so that your reader can understand the unique value that you bring. Career Education has several resources to help you compose these documents. Learn More Celebrating Fellowships! The Wellesley Fellowships team congratulates all our fellowship awardees, nominees, and honorable mentions! In these applying for fellowships and scholarships, these students and graduates dared to articulate their present interests and their hopes and dreams for the future. View the list My professors and peers taught me that wherever you look, there is a question that needs to be explored and that can speak to your meaning in life. When you find one, you must believe you can answer it and realize that you may be surprised by what you discover. Amal Cheema ’17 2017 Watson fellowship recipient Learn more about the Watson Deadlines Events Jobs/Internships Resources Stories #accounting/insurance #advancement #amt #architecture #biotech/lifescience #careeredplacements #coverletter #exploring #faculty/staff #fellowshipstoolkit #highereducation #law #medschool #selfreflection #students #arts/design #bcfm #business/operations #careerpivot #datascience #employers #explore/try #government #gradschool #internshipgrants #interview #preparing #socialsciences #undergraduatefellowship #applying #cegia #consulting #encorecareer #engineering #entertainment #fundedinternship #gettingstarted #internationalaffairs #lawschool #linkedin #postgraduatefellowship #wellesleyopportunity #civicengagement #entrepreneurship #fundraising #industryexpertise #internationalstudent #k12education #law #negotiation #physicalscience #researchingoptions #distinctpopulations #finance #freelance #mentorship #networking #othereducation #publichealth #research/gradschool #sbp #understandingmyself #behavioralhealth #careerexploration #healthprofessions #management/hr #politics/advocacy #rejoiningtheworkforce #research #resume #servicefellowship #fellowships #marketing #media/pr #publishing #studyabroad #sustainability #travelfellowship #nonprofit #reflection #thinktank #professionalism #technology #writing/editing #recruit #socialmedia #careeressentials #socialscience #arts/humanities #science #careeradvancement #Resource Tags – Internships & Grants #Resource Tags - Faculty & Staff #Resource Tags - Recruiting #Other Tags - for grouping purposes only #Resource Tags - Pre-Law #Resource Tags - Communications, Education, Government, International Affairs #Resource Tags - Alumnae #Resource Tags - Science, Behavioral Health, Public Health #Resource Tags - Career Essentials & Exploration #Resource Tags - Health Professions #Resource Tags - Business, Consulting, Finance, Marketing #Resource Tags - Arts, Media, Technology #Resource Tags - Industry Advising #Resource Tags - Career Exploration #Resource Tags - Grad School #Resource Tags - Fellowships & Scholarships Popular Tags #undergraduatefellowship #postgraduatefellowship #fellowshipstoolkit #research/gradschool #servicefellowship #travelfellowship #internationalstudent #science #socialscience #arts/humanities A Brief Introduction to Fellowships and Scholarships Kate Dailinger Fellowships and scholarships offer funding to support a range of purposeful activities, including undergraduate research, language study/other study abroad, self-designed projects, teaching and service, graduate or professional study, or even internships and professional placements. They can open doors for you to things you might not be able to pursue otherwise. There are opportunities for students and graduates of every nationality and at every stage of their careers. What might be the right fit for you? Read More Introduction to Fellowships for Graduates Kate Dailinger Fellowships and scholarships can fund graduate or professional study, purposeful travel, professional placements, self-designed projects, and so much more. They can help you build your experience and qualifications, help you explore a passion, and clarify a path forward. What would you do with a fellowship? Read More Writing a Fellowships Proposal Webinar More Scholarships & Fellowships for Graduate Study (Student Panel, March 2019) More Fellowships and Scholarships for Graduate Study Kate Dailinger There are more fellowships and scholarships than you might think there are to help fund graduate or professional study. It’s helpful to be creative and persistent in your search, and in your applications. This research will give you an overview of some of the fellowships out there, and tips for searching for opportunities. Read More \"Through the Quad fellowship, I’m excited to meet like-minded people to bridge the gap between science and society, creating scientific discoveries that make a positive impact on the world.\" - Vanessa Li ’22 2024 Quad Fellowship Recipient Read More Load more Let’s Talk Contact T. (781) 283-2352 careereducation@wellesley.edu Modulars 400 ( temporary for 2025-2026) 106 Central Street Wellesley, MA 02481 Career Education is available for virtual and in-person appointments . Employers: please visit our recruiting landing page and email recruiting@wellesley.edu with questions. Handshake Disclaimer & Employer Policies Copyright © Trustees of Wellesley College Terms of Use Privacy Policy Press Donate to the Program Handshake Hive Instagram Facebook Linkedin"
    },
