    "https://www.wellesley.edu/careereducation/recruiting-wellesley": {
      "title": "Recruiting",
      "description": "Recruiting at Wellesley | Wellesley Career Education Skip to main content MyWellesley Give Handshake Hive Events ELR Getting Started Employers Faculty Parents About Career Advising Career Exploration Arts, Media, & Technology Business, Consulting, Finance, & Marketing Communication, Education, Government, & International Affairs​ Health Professions Advising Pre-Law Advising Science, Public Health, & Behavioral Health Career Essentials Resources Drop-ins & Peer Career Mentors Graduate School Internships Policies Application Support Short Internship Projects (SHIPs) Wellesley-funded Internships & Grants FAQs Fellowships Fellowships for Undergraduates Fellowships for Graduates Class of 2027 Fellowship Planning Fellowships for International Students Fellowships Browser Civic Engagement Ministrare Peer Leader Office Hours Alumnae BEAM Entrepreneurship Advising Make It Make Cents Wellesley in Business Symposium Recruiting at Wellesley Career Advising Career Exploration Arts, Media, & Technology Business, Consulting, Finance, & Marketing Communication, Education, Government, & International Affairs​ Health Professions Advising Pre-Law Advising Science, Public Health, & Behavioral Health Career Essentials Resources Drop-ins & Peer Career Mentors Graduate School Internships Policies Application Support Short Internship Projects (SHIPs) Wellesley-funded Internships & Grants FAQs Fellowships Fellowships for Undergraduates Fellowships for Graduates Class of 2027 Fellowship Planning Fellowships for International Students Fellowships Browser Civic Engagement Ministrare Peer Leader Office Hours Alumnae BEAM Entrepreneurship Advising Make It Make Cents Wellesley in Business Symposium Handshake Hive Events Deadlines Resources Recruit About Home Recruiting at Wellesley Recruit at Wellesley Thank you for your interest in recruiting at Wellesley College. Our Employer Engagement team in Career Education looks forward to working with you to create a customized recruiting plan, tailored to your company or organization's goals. This can include, but is not limited to, posting and promotion of employment and internship opportunities for students and alumnae, participation in career fairs, facilitation of recruiting events, and conducting student interviews. To participate in recruiting activities, contact recruiting@wellesley.edu . We will partner with you to customize your recruitment and campus engagement plan to meet your needs. All employers who wish to recruit Wellesley students for employment agree to recruit, hire, train and promote individuals without regard to race, color, ethnicity, country of origin, religion, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, disability or socio-economic background/class. Register in Handshake! First Generation 18 % of the incoming class of 2028 are first generation college students Ranking # 4 US News and World Report Liberal Arts College Ranking Language Fluency 52 % of the incoming class of 2028 speak at least one language other than English at home Highly Selective 13 % of applicants were accepted to the incoming class of 2028, representing Wellesley’s high selectivity Learn more about why you should recruit Wellesley students here! Wellesley Recruiting Program Policies Wellesley College has developed the following guidelines to promote an equitable and fair recruiting experience on behalf of our employers as well as our students. Before you begin connecting with Wellesley students, begin by reading this overview and familiarizing yourself with our recruiting expectations and policies. Review Employer Recruiting Policies Ready to Begin? Connect with us on Handshake. Handshake is Wellesley’s career management platform for posting employment opportunities as well as submitting requests to come to campus. Ready to get started? Login to Handshake at the link below, and review our Handshake Employer Approval Guidelines for support. Access Handshake Kate Rettstadt Director, Employer Engagement Ingrid Belete Núñez '90 Assistant Director, Employer Engagement Employer Resources Explore the links below to learn about recruiting on campus, hosting events, connecting on Handshake, and more. Employer Engagement Opportunities Menu (2026–2027) Campus Recruiting Program Policies (Employers) Employer Handshake Resources Off-Campus Employment, Caregiving, and Home-Based Services Policy Employer Engagement Opportunities Menu (2026–2027) Campus Recruiting Program Policies (Employers) Employer Handshake Resources Off-Campus Employment, Caregiving, and Home-Based Services Policy Employer Engagement Opportunities Menu (Fall 2026 & Spring 2027) This menu is available to employer partners who are offering summer internship and/or full-time roles. Learn about our Career Fair, tabling, speed meet-up nights, on-campus recruiting, workshop opportunities, and more. See Menu Wellesley students are extremely motivated with high levels of integrity and work ethic. They take advantage of their available resources to solve complex problems. The students are always asking intelligent questions so they understand the bigger pictures that the analysis they are completing is a part of. Wellesley College's rigorous academics prepare students for challenging internships and provide students with very mature perspectives. Jake Housman Senior Manager, Boston Consulting Group Career Outcomes Rate 97 % of Class of 2023 graduates were employed, accepted to graduate school, participating in a service/volunteer program, or serving in the military within 6 months of graduation 72.26 % employed 23.40 % graduate school 3.4 % still seeking .94 % service program 0 % military Deadlines Events Jobs/Internships Resources Stories #accounting/insurance #advancement #amt #architecture #biotech/lifescience #careeredplacements #coverletter #exploring #faculty/staff #fellowshipstoolkit #highereducation #law #medschool #selfreflection #students #arts/design #bcfm #business/operations #careerpivot #datascience #employers #explore/try #government #gradschool #internshipgrants #interview #preparing #socialsciences #undergraduatefellowship #applying #cegia #consulting #encorecareer #engineering #entertainment #fundedinternship #gettingstarted #internationalaffairs #lawschool #linkedin #postgraduatefellowship #wellesleyopportunity #civicengagement #entrepreneurship #fundraising #industryexpertise #internationalstudent #k12education #law #negotiation #physicalscience #researchingoptions #distinctpopulations #finance #freelance #mentorship #networking #othereducation #publichealth #research/gradschool #sbp #understandingmyself #behavioralhealth #careerexploration #healthprofessions #management/hr #politics/advocacy #rejoiningtheworkforce #research #resume #servicefellowship #fellowships #marketing #media/pr #publishing #studyabroad #sustainability #travelfellowship #nonprofit #reflection #thinktank #professionalism #technology #writing/editing #recruit #socialmedia #careeressentials #socialscience #arts/humanities #science #careeradvancement #Resource Tags – Internships & Grants #Resource Tags - Faculty & Staff #Resource Tags - Recruiting #Other Tags - for grouping purposes only #Resource Tags - Pre-Law #Resource Tags - Communications, Education, Government, International Affairs #Resource Tags - Alumnae #Resource Tags - Science, Behavioral Health, Public Health #Resource Tags - Career Essentials & Exploration #Resource Tags - Health Professions #Resource Tags - Business, Consulting, Finance, Marketing #Resource Tags - Arts, Media, Technology #Resource Tags - Industry Advising #Resource Tags - Career Exploration #Resource Tags - Grad School #Resource Tags - Fellowships & Scholarships Popular Tags #employers #students On-Campus Recruiting Program Policies (Students) Kate Rettstadt Career Education expects all students to abide by the following rules in order to maintain the success and integrity of Wellesley’s recruiting program. Read More Campus Recruiting Program Policies (Employers) Kate Rettstadt Wellesley College has developed the following guidelines to promote an equitable and fair recruiting experience on behalf of our employers as well as our students. It is our expectation that employers who participate in campus recruiting become familiar with the following policies as well as reference these policies throughout the year. Read More Employer Engagement Opportunities Menu (2026–2027) Kate Rettstadt This menu is available to employer partners who are offering summer internship and/or full-time roles. Read More Handshake Disclaimer & Employer Policies Kate Rettstadt Career Education explicitly makes no representations or guarantees about job postings and external events, or the accuracy of the information provided by an employer/fellowship foundation/graduate school. Read More Opportunities for Wellesley Alumnae to Engage with Students via Internships Destiny M. Barletta Learn about the various ways that alums can offer internships to students. Read More Employer Engagement Opportunities Menu (2025–2026) Kate Rettstadt This menu is available to employer partners who are offering summer internship and/or full-time roles. Read More Load more Let’s Talk Contact T. (781) 283-2352 careereducation@wellesley.edu Modulars 400 ( temporary for 2025-2026) 106 Central Street Wellesley, MA 02481 Career Education is available for virtual and in-person appointments . Employers: please visit our recruiting landing page and email recruiting@wellesley.edu with questions. Handshake Disclaimer & Employer Policies Copyright © Trustees of Wellesley College Terms of Use Privacy Policy Press Donate to the Program Handshake Hive Instagram Facebook Linkedin"
