    "https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/wellesley-career-education/": {
      "title": "Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education",
      "description": "Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education | LinkedIn Agree & Join LinkedIn By clicking Continue to join or sign in, you agree to LinkedIn’s User Agreement , Privacy Policy , and Cookie Policy . Sign in to see who you already know at Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education Email or phone Password Show Forgot password? Sign in Sign in with Email or New to LinkedIn? Join now By clicking Continue to join or sign in, you agree to LinkedIn’s User Agreement , Privacy Policy , and Cookie Policy . Skip to main content LinkedIn Top Content People Learning Jobs Games Sign in Join now Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education Higher Education Wellesley Career Education equips and empowers Wellesley students and graduates to engage in an ever-changing world. Follow Report this product About us The mission of the Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education is to equip and empower Wellesley students and graduates to engage, personally and professionally, in an ever-changing world.  With one foot deeply embedded in the rich liberal arts curriculum, and the other in the rapidly changing world of work, Wellesley Career Education ensures that students make connections between curricular and co-curricular experiences, articulate their learning outcomes, and pursue pathways for growth and opportunity. Website https://www1.wellesley.edu/careereducation/ External link for Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education Industry Higher Education Company size 51-200 employees Updates Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education 315 followers 3d Edited Report this post Welcome MUFG to our *new* space in Green Hall for the first on-campus interviews of the semester! MUFG will be back on campus Sept. 15th from 3-6pm for our Fall Job & Internship fair.💥👏  \n🤓 Students can pre-register for the fair now on Handshake: https://lnkd.in/g9ENPfXj PS: Did we mention MUFG sponsors our ice cream truck day of the fair?!🍦 5 Like Comment Share Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education reposted this Katelynne Bazile, MBA 2w Report this post My favorite time of year is when First Gens in Tech Registration opens! Pumped about this year's theme (\"Your Story is Your Superpower\") and what we have in store. Be sure to register so you don't miss out on all of the gems that will be dropped! HubSpot Emerging Talent 9,564 followers 2w Registration is OPEN 🤩\n\nEvery superhero has an origin story. Yours is the reason this event exists 🦸\nHubSpot's First-Gens in Tech 2026 is officially open for registration 🥳\nOn Friday, September 25th, we're bringing together first-generation professionals, new grads, career pivoters, and rising tech trailblazers for a day designed around one truth: your story is your edge.\n\nThis year's theme — The First-Gen Edge: Making Your Story Your Superpower — isn't just a tagline. It's a full-day experience built for where you are right now. Here's what's waiting for you:\n🎯 Breakout sessions built for YOUR career stage\n📝 A live Resume Refresh Hub — 1-on-1 feedback from real industry recruiters\n🤝 Authentic networking (not the awkward kind)\n🤖 Practical AI job-hunting tools with ethical guardrails\n🚀 Direct recruiter touchpoints and real “what’s next” pathways\n\nEvery superhero has a moment when they stop running from their origin story and start owning it. This is yours 💪\n👉 Register now: https://lnkd.in/eES3BcZi First-Gens in Tech hubspot.com 10 Like Comment Share Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education 315 followers 3w Edited Report this post Summer 2027 internships are starting to open! Check out some of these internships at Quantbot Technologies LP 👇 Quantbot Technologies LP 6,182 followers 3w Edited 🚀 Our 2027 internship opportunities are now live! If you're passionate about quant finance, love learning, and want to be part of something dynamic and innovative - we'd love to hear from you. \n\n👉 Apply directly here: https://lnkd.in/eb9T3M_B 3 Like Comment Share Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education 315 followers 3w Report this post Opportunity for a recent grad interested in higher education and using your Japanese language skills! Added bonus: you get to work with another awesome Wellesley alum! Weatherhead Center for International Affairs at Harvard University 2,651 followers 3w Come join us at the Weatherhead Center! We are hiring a staff assistant for our Program on US-Japan Relations: https://lnkd.in/gp2WN2-U Like Comment Share Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education reposted this Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education 315 followers 4w Report this post #WellesleyCollege was recently recognized by LinkedIn News for our summer funded internships in international locations🌎✨ Read more below 👇 LinkedIn News 19,493,656 followers 1mo Edited Internships remain one of the clearest paths from college to a full-time job — and where you go to school can shape how likely you are to land one. \n\nLinkedIn’s latest Top Colleges ranking is out, highlighting the best schools for long-term career success: https://lnkd.in/TopColleges26 . But we also dug into the data to see which colleges have the most grads with internship experience. Caltech takes the No. 1 spot this year, up from No. 2 in 2025. The school helps students get started early: its Career Achievement, Leadership and Exploration (CALE) programs offer resources from mock interviews to salary negotiation techniques. Massachusetts Institute of Technology (No. 2) and Carnegie Mellon University (No. 4) also make the list on the strength of long-standing employer ties across tech and engineering. But the ranking isn’t all STEM — Wellesley College (No. 3) funds more than 250 students' internships around the world each summer.\n\nWeigh in below: What can you gain from an internship that you can’t learn in the classroom? \n\n✍️ Emily Bruck 4 Like Comment Share Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education 315 followers 4w Report this post Here's an opportunity for a part-time internship for a recent grad looking to get involved in community development & local government. Also an opportunity to work with a fellow #Wellesleyalum Sarah Jane Huber :) Sarah Jane Huber 4w Edited We're looking for our next Small Business Support Intern! \n\nBe part of the City of Cambridge 's efforts to:\n➡️ Support small and micro businesses.\n➡️ Promote and strengthen commercial districts.\n➡️ Develop programs and policies.\n➡️ Partner with key industries.\n➡️ Connect constituents to resources. \n\nDevelop your skills in:\n✅ Community engagement and outreach.\n✅ Multidisciplinary planning.\n✅ Program management.\n✅ Data presentation.\n\nApply here: https://lnkd.in/g6FVs8Yz . 2 Like Comment Share Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education 315 followers 4w Report this post #WellesleyCollege was recently recognized by LinkedIn News for our summer funded internships in international locations🌎✨ Read more below 👇 LinkedIn News 19,493,656 followers 1mo Edited Internships remain one of the clearest paths from college to a full-time job — and where you go to school can shape how likely you are to land one. \n\nLinkedIn’s latest Top Colleges ranking is out, highlighting the best schools for long-term career success: https://lnkd.in/TopColleges26 . But we also dug into the data to see which colleges have the most grads with internship experience. Caltech takes the No. 1 spot this year, up from No. 2 in 2025. The school helps students get started early: its Career Achievement, Leadership and Exploration (CALE) programs offer resources from mock interviews to salary negotiation techniques. Massachusetts Institute of Technology (No. 2) and Carnegie Mellon University (No. 4) also make the list on the strength of long-standing employer ties across tech and engineering. But the ranking isn’t all STEM — Wellesley College (No. 3) funds more than 250 students' internships around the world each summer.\n\nWeigh in below: What can you gain from an internship that you can’t learn in the classroom? \n\n✍️ Emily Bruck 4 Like Comment Share Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education 315 followers 1mo Report this post Our Fall Career Fair is an incredible opportunity to meet students in-person on our campus. The past two years, 500+ students have attended this event. #Wellesleyalums in #recruitingroles , are you planning to attend? Questions about this event, email: recruiting@wellesley.edu Kate Rettstadt 1mo 📣 Calling all campus recruiters looking to connect with exceptional talent at a premier women's college! 🎓 Wellesley is seeking additional STEM focused companies to participate in our upcoming Fall Business, Consulting, Finance, and STEM Job & Internship Fair. Register for this event today on Handshake: https://lnkd.in/gQZpadFm 4 4 Comments Like Comment Share Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education 315 followers 2mo Report this post 🎓 If you're pursuing a science degree and you'd like to learn more about Intellectual Property law, consider applying to a fantastic program at global IP law firm Fish & Richardson: School of Fish! \nSchool of Fish participants receive a $1,000 scholarship and assistance with LSAT or Patent Office exam fees. *The deadline to apply is July 15th* https://lnkd.in/g6AnDwrV Explore Intellectual Property Law: Where Science, Engineering, and Technology Meet Law fr.com 1 Comment Like Comment Share Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education 315 followers 2mo Report this post We are seeking new partners from the Greater Boston Chamber of Commerce to participate in our Fall Job & Internship Career Fair and recruit talent from our campus. If you are interested in learning more about this event, please reach out to us at recruiting@wellesley.edu for additional information. Greater Boston Chamber of Commerce 15,571 followers 2mo Join our member, Wellesley College , at their Fall Career Fair on September 15, focused on opportunities in Business, Consulting, Finance and STEM. Register here: https://hubs.la/Q04lDfbx0 Handshake app.joinhandshake.com 1 Like Comment Share Join now to see what you are missing Find people you know at Lulu Chow Wang ’66 Center for Career Education Browse recommended jobs for you View all updates, news, and articles Join now Affiliated pages Wellesley College Higher Education Wellesley, MA The Wagner Centers for Wellesley in the World Higher Education Similar pages Seven Sisters Alum Association Social Networking Platforms Chatham, NJ Lycée Chateaubriand de Rome Primary and Secondary Education Rome, Latium HSM Global Fulfilment Transportation, Logistics, Supply Chain and Storage Millbrook High School Primary and Secondary Education MILLBROOK, New York Palmer High School Palmer, Alaska Villanova College Higher Education King City, ON Granada High School Education Livermore, California Brighter | Employee Loved Software Development Bellevue, WA Maasai Mara University Higher Education Narok, Rift Valley UWC Changshu China Education Administration Programs Changshu, Jiangsu Show more similar pages Show fewer similar pages LinkedIn © 2026 About Accessibility User Agreement Privacy Policy Your California Privacy Choices Cookie Policy Copyright Policy Brand Policy Guest Controls Community Guidelines العربية (Arabic) বাংলা (Bangla) Čeština (Czech) Dansk (Danish) Deutsch (German) Ελληνικά (Greek) English (English) Español (Spanish) فارسی (Persian) Suomi (Finnish) Français (French) हिंदी (Hindi) Magyar (Hungarian) Bahasa Indonesia (Indonesian) Italiano (Italian) עברית (Hebrew) 日本語 (Japanese) 한국어 (Korean) मराठी (Marathi) Bahasa Malaysia (Malay) Nederlands (Dutch) Norsk (Norwegian) ਪੰਜਾਬੀ (Punjabi) Polski (Polish) Português (Portuguese) Română (Romanian) Русский (Russian) Svenska (Swedish) తెలుగు (Telugu) ภาษาไทย (Thai) Tagalog (Tagalog) Türkçe (Turkish) Українська (Ukrainian) Tiếng Việt (Vietnamese) 简体中文 (Chinese (Simplified)) 正體中文 (Chinese (Traditional)) Language"
